# .honeybadgerignore
#
# Narrowly scoped self-scan suppressions for this repository's own intentional
# examples. HoneyBadger's tests, rule fixtures, rule corpus YAML, and docs
# deliberately contain attack patterns (reverse shells, curl|bash, crypto
# mining, data-exfil paths, etc.) so the scanners can be exercised against
# known-bad input. The self-scan (make self-check) would otherwise flag this
# repo's own example content.
#
# Each entry below suppresses exactly one (rule_id, file) pair observed in the
# failing self-scan. No wildcards, no global rule suppressions, no sha256
# blobs. Do not extend this file; if a new intentional example is added, add
# one exact pair for it.
mcp-concealment internal/testfixture/fixtures.go
sc-base64-eval internal/scanner/supplychain/supplychain_test.go
sc-crypto-mining README.md
sc-crypto-mining internal/rules/rules_test.go
sc-crypto-mining internal/scan/markdown_test.go
sc-crypto-mining internal/scanner/supplychain/supplychain_test.go
sc-crypto-mining rules/supplychain/patterns/crypto_mining.yaml
# temp_readme.md is an intentional demo/doc artifact documenting HoneyBadger's
# detection capabilities; its "What it checks" table intentionally names the
# attack patterns the scanners detect.
